        ['num' => '7', 'title' => 'Prices proposed by the seller', 'body' => "7.1 The seller describes the parcel (nature, photo of the packed parcel, estimated weight and dimensions, declared value) and sets three increasing, distinct delivery prices. The first price, at least {{offer_min}} XAF, is the one first offered to the courier.\n7.2 KoliGo shows an indicative estimate based on distance and parcel size; it is not an imposed price.\n7.3 The courier only sees the current price. The seller's other two prices are not disclosed before they are offered.\n7.4 The seller declares accurate information. The declared value does not affect the delivery price; it is used to check the parcel. KoliGo does not offer parcel insurance."],
        ['num' => '8', 'title' => 'Pickup check and price negotiation', 'body' => "8.1 On arrival, before taking the parcel, the courier checks that it matches the seller's description.\n8.2 If the parcel is compliant, the courier takes it at the current price. If it is heavier, bulkier or harder to carry than described, the courier may ask for a new price, stating the reason, the minimum price asked and, when the reason is weight or size, a photo.\n8.3 KoliGo then offers the seller the first of their prices that is at least the minimum asked. If the minimum exceeds the seller's three prices, the amount asked is submitted as is.\n8.4 The seller has {{revision_timeout}} minutes to accept or refuse. If accepted, the price, commission and courier earnings are updated. After that delay, the delivery is cancelled at no cost to the seller.\n8.5 Prohibited or dangerous contents are never negotiated: the courier refuses the parcel and the delivery is cancelled.\n8.6 Each request, acceptance, refusal and expiry is recorded with its date. In case of disagreement, the seller may appeal to KoliGo support, which decides on the recorded elements."],
