        ['num' => '10', 'title' => 'Declaration incidents and suspension', 'body' => "10.1 A declaration incident is recorded when the courier finds at pickup a weight, size or value that does not match the seller's declaration, or prohibited or dangerous contents.\n10.2 An incident becomes confirmed when the seller answers the proposed correction (accepts or refuses) or when KoliGo confirms it after review. An incident cancelled by KoliGo does not count.\n10.3 After {{strike_threshold}} confirmed incidents, the seller account is suspended: the seller can no longer publish deliveries but keeps access to their history and may appeal.\n10.4 A warning is sent before suspension. Only KoliGo can lift a suspension, after reviewing the appeal or speaking with the seller."],
        ['num' => '11', 'title' => 'Prohibited items and monitoring of messages', 'body' => "11.1 It is forbidden to have KoliGo carry narcotics, weapons and ammunition, explosives, toxic or dangerous goods, counterfeit money or forged documents, protected species (ivory, pangolin, etc.) or any other item whose possession or transport is illegal in Cameroon.
11.2 The courier may refuse any parcel they consider suspicious or dangerous; the seller alone is responsible for the contents they declare.
